I have a further question about the data imputation procedure. Based on the explanations provided on this page <https://wadpac.github.io/GGIR/articles/chapter6_DataImputation.html>, the non-wear periods or segments with clipping problems will not be imputed if do.impute is set as FALSE, and that the recorded values are kept as they are and not imputed or omitted. Does this mean that the identified non-wear periods (eg. 10-10.30am) will still be included in the analysis even though they have been flagged as non-wear and treated as invalid? And will the initial metric value (or zero) be included in the data file for further processing?

