>From reading the GGIR docs (Chapter 6 <https://wadpac.github.io/GGIR/articles/chapter6_DataImputation.html>), I understand that epoch-level ENMO is imputed using data from other days (if non-wear is detected in that epoch AND there is a sufficient number of valid days to derive the imputed value from).

Can I assume this is also the case when it comes to lux data? To be clear, I am referring to the csv files in /meta/ms5.outraw/, and the data that is found in the lightpeak column.

